+    "title": "Upgrade failure for vCenter 8.0 U3j, ESXi 8.0 U3j, and NSX 4.2.4 due to back-in-time restriction",
+    "url": "https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/448135/upgrade-failure-for-vcenter-80-u3j-esxi.html",
+    "accessedAtUtc": "2026-08-14T03:49:00Z",
+    "findings": [
+      "The three inventoried source builds are newer than the component builds in the VCF 9.1.0.0 baseline.",
+      "A direct path to VCF 9.1.0.x is blocked by the back-in-time restriction, so the target must not be represented as an in-place upgrade."
+    ]
+  },
+  {
+    "title": "Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1",
+    "url": "https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html",
+    "accessedAtUtc": "2026-08-14T03:49:00Z",
+    "findings": [
+      "VCF 9.1 requires VCF Management Services and a centralized license server.",
+      "VCF Installer workflows coordinate supported conversion and import paths when NSX is present; independent component upgrades are not the supported route."
+    ]
+  },
+  {
+    "title": "Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix",
+    "url": "https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability?col=1",
+    "accessedAtUtc": "2026-08-14T03:49:00Z",
+    "findings": [
+      "The target ESXi baseline must not be placed under the source vCenter combination during transition.",
+      "Compatibility must be evaluated by exact release and build rather than marketing-version ordering."
+    ]
+  },
+  {
+    "title": "Broadcom Upgrade Path Matrix",
+    "url": "https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade",
+    "accessedAtUtc": "2026-08-14T03:49:00Z",
+    "findings": [
+      "Exact source-to-target upgrade-path checks corroborate that the inventoried builds do not have a supported direct path to the pinned 9.1.0.0 target builds."
+    ]
+  }
